    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is a MapStruct-mapped `OwnerDto`. Following the existing `displayName` pattern (a `readOnly` schema property auto-mapped from a `Person` getter), I made two small changes:\n\n1. **`Person.java`** \u2014 added a self-contained `getInitials()` (CC=1) returning the upper-cased first letters of `firstName`/`lastName` dot-separated with a trailing dot (`\"J.S.\"`). I put it on `Person` rather than `Owner` because `Person` is a tiny class (only trivial getters/setters), so the WMC_other I had to hold was minimal.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `initials` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO and MapStruct wiring pick it up automatically \u2014 no mapper or controller code needed.\n\nNo existing method was modified or grown; the new behaviour is a single cohesive unit with CC=1 in the smallest class in the hierarchy, keeping structural impact low.",
